---
import HeldScene from '../HeldScene.astro';
import { forum } from '../../data/site.js';
---
{/*
  The homepage's one Forum scene — and the SITE'S ONE HELD SCENE.

  WHY THE HOLD IS SPENT HERE. refs/MOTION-FINDINGS.md measured the reference
  and found one structural idea we did not have: the subject is held in place
  while the environment changes around it and successive text beats fade
  through. Hold the visual, move the type. `HeldScene` was built for that and
  then shipped nowhere — it existed only in `src/pages/_lab.astro`, which is
  underscore-prefixed and does not build, so the site had ZERO held scenes and
  the finding was unspent.

  Of the six full-bleed photographs on this site, this is the only one that is
  not already carrying an exception:

    hero.jpg       homepage  holds the four 2026 partners by name inside the
                             first screen; pinning it puts the Institute's only
                             credential two viewport heights below the fold
    pilot-maternal homepage  the Stake — one sentence ranged right into the one
                             patch of empty wall the crop was chosen to leave.
                             HeldScene sets its beats in a band at the FOOT of
                             the frame; pinning that scene replaces it
    forum.jpg      /forum/   the masthead, whose baseline is registered to
                             where the breakwater crosses the frame
    institute.jpg  /institute/ the 40-star flag on the committee room's axis
    institute.jpg  /people/  the turn from navy to cream
    forum.jpg      HERE      an eyebrow, a bridge line, a name and a link, laid
                             over a picture that scrolls past exactly like every
                             other frame on the site

  It is also the scene refs/MOTION-FINDINGS.md nominates ("the Forum, whose
  photograph is the most evocative asset the Institute has"). The /forum/ page
  itself cannot host the hold: its copy is fully spent — masthead, claim,
  ledger, close — and there is no beat left there that is not a duplicate of a
  section 1,000px above it. Here every string the hold needs is already in this
  scene, in `site.js`, so the hold costs the homepage no new words.

  ONE PER SITE. `[data-hold]` appears exactly once in `dist/`. If a second
  scene wants this, one of the two is not the scene its page is about.

  WHAT CHANGED, EXACTLY. Nothing in the copy. `forum.access` was the eyebrow
  and is the eyebrow; `forum.name` was the h2 and is the h2 (via `headingId`,
  so the page keeps its outline); `forum.place` was the bridge under the name
  and is now that beat's note; `forum.line` was the body line under the rule
  and is the second beat; `forum.cta` was the link and is the coda. The name
  steps down from --step-poster to --step-head, which is what a beat is — the
  scene buys 2,400px of held photograph and a navy → lit → navy arc for 33px
  of type, and the ladder still has the hero at 126 and six posters at 86.

  arc="lift". The scene arrives out of the Pilots ledger — this page's one
  remaining event-free run — opens to the lit harbour, and closes back into
  navy to hand the People wall a dark edge to start from. `fall` would strand
  the ledger's flat navy against a flat navy opening; `rise` would light the
  People wall's own head.

  The two location strings still do two jobs and still do not share a corner:
  `forum.place` — the CONVENING — rides the name's beat; the photograph's own
  credit — Block Island, Rhode Island — is in the opposite corner in the dim
  credit register — top-right, on the eyebrow's line and the full width of
  the frame away from the event line at the foot, which is the same diagonal
  the /forum/ masthead uses. HeldScene's own default is bottom-right, and on
  this frame that put the two location strings in the same foot band, and put
  the credit on water that is lit for the middle two thirds of the hold.
  refs/PHOTO-FACTS.md.
*/}
<HeldScene
  src={forum.image}
  alt="A harbour at dusk: moored sailboats inside a stone breakwater under a blue-hour sky."
  eyebrow={forum.access}
  headingId="forum-h"
  hold={1.9}
  holdSm={1.6}
  focal="52% 52%"
  focalSm="46% 52%"
  credit={forum.credit}
  creditPos="top-right"
  noteAs="bridge"
  arc="lift"
  beats={[
    { line: forum.name, note: forum.place },
    { line: forum.line },
  ]}
>
  <a slot="coda" class="label label--lit tap forum__more" href="/forum/">
    {forum.cta}
    <svg class="arrow" viewBox="0 0 22 10" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 1l5 4-5 4M21 5H0" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" fill="none"/></svg>
  </a>
</HeldScene>

<style>
  /* The coda link keeps the register it had before the scene was held: the
     .label voice at link brightness, with the arrow and the underline that
     draws in from the left. This is a state on an existing class, not a new
     rung. The clip-path wipe HeldScene runs on the coda needs an inline-flex
     box to clip, which is what this is. */
  .forum__more {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.9ch;
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--fg);
    padding-block: 0.5rem;
  }
  .forum__more:hover :global(.arrow) { transform: translateX(4px); }
  .forum__more::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0.1em; height: 1px;
    background: currentColor; transform: scaleX(0); transform-origin: right;
    transition: transform 520ms var(--ease-out);
  }
  .forum__more:hover::after { transform: scaleX(1); transform-origin: left; }
</style>
